    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0452" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 895.155D22/5.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 140.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 17, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has read your No. 509 of
                    January 29, 1912,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d480-f1"/> with reference to the
                    suggestion that the President of the United States be made the Honorary
                    President, and Count Moltke and you Honorary Vice Presidents in connection with
                    the presentation to Denmark of a tract of land bought by the Danish-American
                    Society <pb facs="0453" n="337" xml:id="pg337"/> in Jutland, and in reply
                    informs you that the President has accepted the invitation of the
                    Danish-American Society.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
